<title>UK: Queue for Panama Canal could grow to 100 vessels.</title>
<headline>Queue for Panama Canal could grow to 100 vessels.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The queue of vessels awaiting transit through the Panama Canal, partly blocked by a tug, could grow to 100 vessels with 4-5 days waiting time before the tug is removed, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said.</p>
<p>The tug San Pablo II is partly blocking the entrance to the seaward side of the east lane of Miraflores locks reducing daily Panama Canal capacity to about 33 vessels. Operations for removal and salvage of the tug have already commenced and are estimated to take about 10 days.</p>
<p>The queue of vessels awaiting transit for Balboa and Cristobal on Thursday was 62.</p>
</text>
